:: Profit Party [event main_quest] {"position":"5075,500","size":"100,100"}
/* Quest "The Profit Party" (main_profitParty), STAGE1_PROPOSAL.md 4.9. The company account is in the black. Friday evening,
   pizza and drinks in the office. I announce the Catalyst (the V2 plan: a unit that adapts to each person, in the Veil version
   of the story). A drunk $ethan.name gives his "best boss I've ever had" speech and jokes about "my piece", and I give him a
   token 2 percent, no choice (the quest's set sets $ethan.equity). $marketingOwner.name has sent word that she knows
   $investor.callName, who could open the door to $retailChain.name: the first mention. A small crack: $brian.name asks, uh,
   what the Catalyst is for, and gets the Veil answer. A line changes with $flags.dariusBroughtIn.
   The quest's set unlocks project_company_catalyst. */
<<silent>><<SetBackground $locations[13].img>><</silent>>
The account crossed into the black on Wednesday at 2:14 in the afternoon, when the second gym payment cleared. I know the exact minute because I was sitting there refreshing the banking app, which is more or less what I've been doing with that number for months, like standing over a pot and waiting for it to boil.

So on Friday at five the office closes early and turns into a party. $mom.callName ordered the pizza, which means there's a salad nobody asked for. $ethan.name brought the drinks, which means there's a bottle of something blue nobody can identify. $sister.callName made a banner out of printer paper and tape that says WE'RE NOT BROKE!!! and hung it over the coffee machine, slightly crooked, and nobody has the heart to straighten it.

/* MEDIA: images/events/profit_party/office.jpg | The office after hours, pizza boxes on the desks, a crooked hand-made banner reading WE'RE NOT BROKE over the coffee machine, everyone holding cups */

<<linkreplace "Join the party">>
<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $ethan, text: "There he is, the guy who signs our checks! Somebody get this man a cup of the blue stuff." },
{ who: $player, text: "Okay, but what actually is the blue stuff?" },
{ who: $ethan, text: "It was on sale and it's festive. I stopped reading the label after that." },
{ text: "$mom.callName hands me a cup of the blue stuff and, a second later, a plate with two slices and a pile of salad on it, and gives me a look that says the salad isn't optional." },
{ who: $mom, text: "Eat something green, honey, you've had nothing but coffee since Tuesday, and don't think I didn't notice." },
{ who: $sister, text: "Before you say anything about the banner, yes, I know it's crooked, and it's staying crooked. It has character." },
{ who: $player, text: "I wasn't going to say anything. I think it's the nicest thing in this office, honestly." },
{ who: $sister, text: "Obviously it is. I just wanted to hear you admit it." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

For an hour it's just a party. $brian.name and $ethan.name argue about whether pineapple is a vegetable. <<if $flags.dariusBroughtIn === true>>$darius.name, in his new title and a slightly loosened tie, is explaining the gym numbers to $mom.callName, who is pretending to follow and doing it very well.<<else>>$darius.name stands near the window with a cup he hasn't touched, polite and pleasant, and every so often I catch him watching the room the way he watches a spreadsheet.<</if>> $sister.callName dances with $mom.callName to something on $ethan.name's phone, badly, both of them laughing too hard to finish.

<<linkreplace "Make an announcement">>
At half past six I tap my cup with a pen. It's a paper cup, so it doesn't work, and $ethan.name does it for me by putting two fingers in his mouth and whistling.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "Thanks. Okay, I'll keep this short, because I know $ethan.name is going to give a speech later whether we want one or not." },
{ who: $ethan, text: "And it's going to be a great speech, so pace yourselves." },
{ who: $player, text: "A few months ago this company was me, a prototype and a broom closet two floors down. Now there are six of us, three products and a bank account I can actually look at without feeling sick, and that's because of you guys. So, thank you. I mean it." },
{ text: "$mom.callName puts her hand over her heart, and $sister.callName whoops." },
{ who: $player, text: "So, what's next. The Veil works on a whole room, and everybody in it gets the same thing, which is good, but it's pretty blunt. The next one is going to learn what each person responds to and support that. One unit, and a different effect for every single person in the room." },
{ who: $player, text: "We're calling it the Catalyst." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

$ethan.name throws both hands in the air. $brian.name has gone very still, the way he does when he's already thinking about the hardware. <<if $flags.dariusBroughtIn === true>>$darius.name gives me a small nod, like a man who just saw the next chapter in a book he's helping to write.<<else>>$darius.name writes something down on a napkin.<</if>>

<<linkreplace "Let them react">>
<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $mom, text: "Oh, the Catalyst, that sounds so scientific, sweetie. So it's like the Veil, only nicer?" },
{ who: $player, text: "Sort of. Smarter, more than nicer." },
{ who: $sister, text: "I want to name the colors. I already have the first one, it's called 'Seafoam Breakthrough', and I'm not taking questions." },
{ text: "And then, quietly, from the edge of the group, holding a slice of pizza he's forgotten to eat:" },
{ who: $brian, text: "Um. What's it for, though? Exactly?" },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

He asks the floor near my shoes instead of me. As far as I can remember, it's the first time $brian.name has ever asked me what a device does instead of how it does it.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "Same thing the Veil does, really. Calm, focus, people feeling comfortable, just tuned to each person instead of the whole room. If somebody's anxious they get a little calmer, if they're tired they get a bit more energy. Think of it as a really good thermostat, only for moods." },
{ who: $brian, text: "Hm. A thermostat. Okay, yeah, that makes sense." },
{ text: "He nods and finally takes a bite of his pizza. I can't tell whether he believes me, and I get the feeling he can't either." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

<<linkreplace "$ethan.name's speech">>
At eight, three cups of the blue stuff in, $ethan.name climbs onto a chair. $mom.callName tells him to get down before he breaks his neck. He doesn't.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $ethan, text: "Okay, everybody shut up for a second, I've prepared remarks." },
{ who: $sister, text: "You have not prepared remarks." },
{ who: $ethan, text: "I have prepared remarks in my heart." },
{ text: "He puts his hand on his heart and almost falls off the chair. $brian.name steadies it without being asked." },
{ who: $ethan, text: "I've had three bosses in my life, if you count the car wash. Two of them were idiots, and the third one was worse, because he was a smart idiot. And then this guy, my old lab partner, the one who taped a baby monitor to a bike helmet and called it a science project, calls me out of nowhere after a whole year, and..." },
{ text: "He stops and looks at me across the room, and for a second, through all the blue stuff, he's completely serious." },
{ who: $ethan, text: "...and he's the best boss I've ever had. That's it, that's the whole speech. There was more, but that was the important part." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

Everybody cheers, $mom.callName wipes her eyes, and $sister.callName films the whole thing on her phone. Above us the vent hums along at its usual setting, like it does every working day, and I don't let myself think about that for more than a second.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $ethan, text: "Oh, and also! As the guy who wrote most of the code, I'd like to formally remind the boss that he still owes me my piece." },
{ text: "He's grinning when he says it, and everyone laughs, because it's been a running joke since his first week. He's still looking at me, though." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

<<linkreplace "Give him his piece">>
<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "Okay. How does two percent sound?" },
{ who: $ethan, text: "Wait, what?" },
{ who: $player, text: "Two percent of the company. I'll have the paperwork on your desk Monday morning. I told you you'd get your piece, didn't I?" },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

For a second the whole room is quiet. $ethan.name stands on his chair with his cup in one hand and his mouth slightly open, and for once in his life he doesn't have a joke ready.

Then he gets down off the chair, very carefully, walks across the office, and hugs me so hard my cup of blue stuff goes all over both of us.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $ethan, text: "You're an idiot, you know that? Two percent. I'm going to frame the paperwork and hang it over my desk." },
{ who: $player, text: "Dude, you're getting blue stuff in my ear." },
{ who: $ethan, text: "Shut up, I'm having a moment here." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

It's two percent of a company whose most valuable product is hidden in the ceiling, and he'll never see the books that say what it's really worth. But as far as he's concerned, it's the first promise anyone has kept to him since he started working, and I'm glad I can give him that, especially when it costs me so little.

<<linkreplace "Later">>
Later, when the pizza's gone and $ethan.name is asleep on the couch in the meeting room with the banner over him like a blanket, $mom.callName finds me by the window.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $mom, text: "Oh, honey, I almost forgot, $marketingOwner.name called this afternoon to congratulate you on the gyms. Don't ask me how she'd heard already, that woman hears about everything before it happens." },
{ who: $mom, text: "And then she said she knows a man, $investor.callName, who sits on a lot of boards and is apparently very close with the people at $retailChain.name. She said, and I wrote it down so I'd get it right..." },
{ text: "She takes a folded sticky note out of her cardigan pocket and reads it carefully." },
{ who: $mom, text: "'If your boy wants a national account, $investor.name is the door. Doors like that don't come free.' She called you my boy. I thought that was sweet, so I didn't correct her." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

I take the sticky note from her and look at the name for a while. Out on the street, the neon sign of the bar two blocks down flickers on.

A national chain would mean hundreds of stores, and thousands of rooms with something of mine in the ceiling. I fold the note and put it in my pocket, and I'm still trying to guess what kind of price a door like that has when $sister.callName comes over to ask whether anyone's sober enough to drive $ethan.name home.

<<UpdateStat "+" "Morale" 6>>
<<UpdateStat "+" "Reputation" 3>>
<<UpdateStat "+" "MomRelation" 1>>
<<UpdateStat "+" "SisterRelation" 1>>
<<run State.variables.ethan.stats.morale = State.variables.ethan.stats.max.morale>>
<<NextQuest $player>>
<<run Notification.show("New project available: " + $company.devices.valenxCatalyst.name, { type: Notification.INFORMATION })>>
<<ReturnFromEvent>>
<</linkreplace>>
<</linkreplace>>
<</linkreplace>>
<</linkreplace>>
<</linkreplace>>
<</linkreplace>>
